---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/ui-remediation-r7.css';
const title = 'About Stable or Gone — Stablecoin History Archive';
const description = 'Stable or Gone documents stablecoin launches, lifecycle status, issuer and protocol relationships, depegs, recoveries, migrations, wind-downs, reserve disclosures, redemption terms, and sources.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/about/">
  <article class="r7-page r7-about-page" data-r7-page="about">
    <header class="r7-masthead">
      <div class="r7-masthead-copy"><p class="r7-eyebrow">Project / about</p><h1>Why Stable or Gone exists</h1><p class="r7-lead">Stablecoins change over time. Stable or Gone preserves those changes as source-backed records rather than reducing each asset to a current price, market cap, or one-word label.</p></div>
      <dl class="r7-facts"><div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>History and current state</dd></div><div><dt>Unit</dt><dd>Stablecoin entity</dd></div><div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Claim-scoped sources</dd></div><div><dt>Operation</dt><dd>Independent project</dd></div></dl>
    </header>

    <section class="r7-section"><div class="r7-section-heading"><h2>Purpose</h2><p>A stablecoin’s present label rarely explains how it launched, changed, recovered, migrated, wound down, or failed.</p></div><p>Stable or Gone keeps identity, lifecycle status, organizations, dated events, reserves, redemption terms, deployments, Evidence, and known unknowns in one historical registry. The aim is a reviewable record of change, not a score or recommendation.</p></section>

    <section class="r7-section"><div class="r7-section-heading"><h2>Coverage and exclusions</h2><p>The registry includes active and historical stablecoins but deliberately excludes live trading and advisory functions.</p></div><dl class="r7-row-list"><div><dt>Covered</dt><dd>Stablecoin entities, issuer and protocol relationships, material events, reserve and redemption profiles, chain deployments, source identities, and unresolved public-information gaps.</dd></div><div><dt>Not covered</dt><dd>Live prices, market-cap rankings, exchange order books, wallet support, redemptions, account recovery, legal advice, tax advice, or investment recommendations.</dd></div><div><dt>Incomplete records</dt><dd>Some assets have thin or conflicting public documentation. Missing values and open questions remain visible instead of being replaced with estimates.</dd></div></dl></section>

    <section class="r7-section"><div class="r7-section-heading"><h2>Review process</h2><p>Records are assembled from scoped public sources and are changed through reviewable repository updates.</p></div><dl class="r7-row-list r7-about-process"><div><dt></dt><dd><strong>Identify the entity and claim.</strong> Separate the stablecoin, organizations, dated event, and exact field being reviewed.</dd></div><div><dt></dt><dd><strong>Collect Evidence.</strong> Prefer official notices, reports, regulator documents, repositories, archives, and direct on-chain references; use independent reporting for context.</dd></div><div><dt></dt><dd><strong>Classify conservatively.</strong> Current state, event history, confidence, and unresolved questions remain separate.</dd></div><div><dt></dt><dd><strong>Validate and publish.</strong> Automated contracts check structure and links; reviewed changes are merged with a public history.</dd></div></dl><p><a href="/methodology/">Read the full methodology</a>.</p></section>

    <section class="r7-section"><div class="r7-section-heading"><h2>Operator and independence</h2><p>Stable or Gone is maintained by badjoke-lab as an independent historical-data project.</p></div><dl class="r7-row-list"><div><dt>Editorial control</dt><dd>Inclusion, wording, confidence, and status labels are determined by the published methodology and available Evidence.</dd></div><div><dt>Funding</dt><dd>Optional support may help fund research and maintenance. It does not buy listings, favorable treatment, faster corrections, or status changes.</dd></div><div><dt>Corrections</dt><dd>Anyone may submit a source-backed correction, missing record, or broken-link report. Acceptance requires verification.</dd></div></dl><div class="r7-secondary-links"><a href="/contact/">Submit a correction</a><a href="/support/">Support maintenance</a><a href="https://github.com/badjoke-lab/stable-or-gone" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View repository</a></div></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
